WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.522
Elmi Guray Academy.

2
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:04.456
Lesson 9.

3
00:00:04.456 --> 00:00:07.459
GitHub Copilot Core Features.

4
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:14.749
Lesson Introduction In Lesson 8, we introduced GitHub Copilot as an AI coding assistant.

5
00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:32.444
In this lesson, we will focus more closely on how Copilot becomes part of a developer's working environment, how developers access it, why account authentication is required, and why subscription limits should be understood before depending heavily on AI coding tools.

6
00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:41.520
We will use Visual Studio Code as our main example because it provides a common environment for learning AI-assisted software development.

7
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:50.433
Learning Objectives By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: Explain how GitHub Copilot connects to a development environment.

8
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:54.903
Understand the difference between an editor and an extension.

9
00:00:54.903 --> 00:00:58.857
Identify important Copilot capabilities.

10
00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:02.539
Understand why a GitHub account is required.

11
00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:08.082
Understand why AI coding services may have usage plans and limits.

12
00:01:08.082 --> 00:01:12.444
Recognize that pricing and plan details may change.

13
00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:16.425
Understand the basic Copilot setup workflow.

14
00:01:16.425 --> 00:01:19.876
Technical Explanation — English 1.

15
00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:29.196
Copilot Inside the Development Environment GitHub Copilot adds AI-assisted development capabilities to supported coding environments.

16
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:37.552
Depending on the editor or IDE, Copilot may be available through an extension, integration, or built-in feature.

17
00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:44.821
This means the developer does not always need to leave the coding environment to ask an AI tool for help.

18
00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:47.579
2. What Is an Extension?

19
00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:54.699
An extension is an additional software component that adds new capabilities to an existing application.

20
00:01:54.699 --> 00:02:01.533
For example, Visual Studio Code can support extensions for: Programming languages.

21
00:02:01.533 --> 00:02:03.761
Debugging tools.

22
00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:05.582
Formatting.

23
00:02:05.582 --> 00:02:07.675
Git integration.

24
00:02:07.675 --> 00:02:10.324
AI coding assistance.

25
00:02:10.324 --> 00:02:14.223
An extension does not normally replace the editor.

26
00:02:14.223 --> 00:02:17.824
Instead, it adds functionality to it.

27
00:02:17.824 --> 00:02:26.642
3. Main AI Capabilities A Copilot-enabled development environment may provide several forms of AI assistance.

28
00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:32.308
Capability Purpose Code Completion Suggests code while the developer is typing.

29
00:02:32.308 --> 00:02:37.104
Code Generation Generates code from an instruction or prompt.

30
00:02:37.104 --> 00:02:42.783
AI Chat Lets developers ask questions about code and software problems.

31
00:02:42.783 --> 00:02:48.300
Agentic Assistance Can attempt several related steps toward a development goal.

32
00:02:48.300 --> 00:03:04.821
4. Code Completion Suppose you start writing: function greetStudent(name) { An AI coding assistant may predict the next part: function greetStudent(name) { return "Welcome, " + name; } This is called a code suggestion or code completion.

33
00:03:04.821 --> 00:03:09.196
You should still understand the suggestion before accepting it.

34
00:03:09.196 --> 00:03:16.044
5. Code Generation Instead of starting the code yourself, you can also describe what you need.

35
00:03:16.044 --> 00:03:23.069
Example prompt: Create a JavaScript function that checks whether a quiz score is 70 or higher.

36
00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:31.357
Possible generated code: function hasPassed(score) { return score >= 70; } 6.

37
00:03:31.357 --> 00:03:37.403
AI Chat AI chat provides a conversational way to work with the coding assistant.

38
00:03:37.403 --> 00:03:40.650
You might ask: Explain this file.

39
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.069
Why am I getting this error?

40
00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:46.927
How can I make this function easier to understand?

41
00:03:46.927 --> 00:03:49.672
Write tests for this function.

42
00:03:49.672 --> 00:03:53.843
Explain the difference between let and const. 7.

43
00:03:53.843 --> 00:03:59.767
AI Agents More advanced AI coding systems may work in an agent-like way.

44
00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:07.145
Instead of producing only one answer, an AI agent may attempt several related development steps.

45
00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:16.533
For example: Create a registration form, add validation, check the existing project structure, and explain the files you changed.

46
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:24.726
This type of assistance can be powerful, but the developer should review important actions before trusting the final result.

47
00:04:24.726 --> 00:04:30.704
8. GitHub Account and Sign-In GitHub Copilot is connected to GitHub services.

48
00:04:30.704 --> 00:04:38.340
Therefore, the developer normally needs to authenticate with a GitHub account before using Copilot features.

49
00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:43.123
Authentication means proving to the service which account you are using.

50
00:04:43.123 --> 00:04:47.702
A typical flow may look like: Open Visual Studio Code.

51
00:04:47.702 --> 00:04:51.248
Open the Copilot feature or extension.

52
00:04:51.248 --> 00:04:53.680
Choose the sign-in option.

53
00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.968
Authenticate using your GitHub account.

54
00:04:56.968 --> 00:05:00.066
Return to the development environment.

55
00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:03.694
Confirm that Copilot features are available.

56
00:05:03.694 --> 00:05:12.240
9. Plans, Usage Limits, and Cost AI coding services can have different access plans and usage limits.

57
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.435
Some users may have limited access while heavier use may require a paid subscription.

58
00:05:18.435 --> 00:05:20.650
The exact names,

59
00:05:20.836 --> 00:05:25.881
prices, limits, and available features can change over time.

60
00:05:25.831 --> 00:05:33.317
Therefore, an AI Developer should never build permanent assumptions around an old price or plan name.

61
00:05:33.317 --> 00:05:39.852
Always check the current official service information before paying for an AI development tool.

62
00:05:39.852 --> 00:05:46.646
10. Usage Planning Developers should think about how heavily they intend to use AI tools.

63
00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:55.056
Occasional code assistance may require less usage than running AI agents frequently across a large software project.

64
00:05:55.056 --> 00:05:58.466
This is one reason usage limits matter.

